+# N24 conditional protected validation protocol v1
+
+CPU preparation while the frozen N24 Dev cohort runs; no protected execution authority. This protocol cannot promote an incomplete, invalid, interrupted or rejected Dev cohort.
+
+## Entry
+
+Require all40 first-valid, independently audited C0/Q0/N23/N24 Dev cells from plan SHA886c676f72a9f57a6d06f28ce55f70088fbc5761cbcfbf0bfc6ef21a95b37bb3, candidate N24>=5/10 and>=each comparator, and the existing substantive QD/ED, compute, source, safety and cost gates. Root must independently review the immutable actual result, terminal ledger, supervisor status, accepted-cell lineage and same-process native audit receipts. N23 is an ablation comparator only. Partial/futility/invalid results forbid this route.
+
+## Immutable science and source bridge
+
+Preserve N24/C0/Q0 scientific profiles and every frozen core/main/config/provider/native arithmetic/evidence audit file from Dev commit3b7afa02757eb3519d95547e4b6e6e939f7068f2 and all230 source records. Keep720 simulator actions,20Hz,8-action chunks and176 canonical candidates/11 batches,10 parent rounds. N24 local cache/parent rescue and original QD/ED/final-selection semantics cannot change. No new preflight, scoring, model, simulator branch or privileged feedback. Preserve the previously settled strict native arithmetic proof via the actual reviewed source bridge; never represent validation source as identical to Dev source.
+
+Only evaluation/identity/accounting files may change after Dev promotion and explicit root review/integration. New validation modules must be independently frozen. The shared worker may add only an explicit validation-context routing branch inside validate_context; run_worker, verify_receipt and every other existing worker function remain byte-identical to Dev. Existing Dev checks must remain intact. No function-code cloning or shared-global replacement for the new routing. Root reviews an exact source bridge, not a broad file allowlist. The Dev source and its live controller must remain untouched during CPU preparation.
+
+## Closed identities and capacity
+
+Freeze60 primary cells: two10-task blocks, backend task order0..9, C0/Q0/N24 per task. Choose the first unused complete preregistered cohort c1..c4 solely from frozen metadata, reconciled exposure registry and dispatched identity metadata under private locks. Any prior dispatch/exposure consumes its entire cohort regardless of arm, validity or outcome. Never inspect protected outcomes to choose identities. No partial block, alternate seed or outcome-based replacement. This is same-layout seed robustness, not new-layout generalization.
+
+One protected cohort per N24 candidate. Maximum62 whole-episode dispatches including at most2 typed recoveries, at most1 recovery per cell;32 local GPU-process hours;1800 seconds plus40 seconds cleanup per episode; one serial GPU7 with the same frozen UUID/EGL/runtime binding. Cumulative478 attempts/100 GPU hours, buckets51 baseline/187 development/180 validation/40 formal/20 recovery and32h validation/12h formal reservations remain unchanged. All historical costs remain. Full primary capacity, up to2 recoveries, local32h ceiling and remaining formal reserve must fit before release and every dispatch. This protocol adds no budget and authorizes no transfer.
+
+## Recovery and accounting
+
+Use the exact N24 Dev narrowly typed sole Codex timeout classifier and its already-reviewed serialized zero-guided compatibility. Only a terminal invalid primary with exactly one codex_timeout, no completed turn/agent message for that call, all other Stage calls successful, complete non-derivative validity evidence and accepted independent native audit can qualify. Bind eligibility to failed terminal/source/runtime/profile/native/Stage/cost evidence and immutable identity. Whole-episode recovery uses a new recovery-bucket attempt with retry_of and identical source/seed/init/profile/provider settings. Preserve the original invalidity and all costs; first-valid selection only. Unknown token usage remains null/partial. No per-Stage retry until a desired response.
+
+Never retry a valid task failure, another API error, missing data/proof, model/action/source/nonfinite/safety fault, process interruption or whole-worker timeout. Failed recovery or any other invalidity terminates this validation as INVALID. An invalid validation is not permission to restart or select another cohort for N24.
+
+## Gates and output
+
+All60 accepted audited cells are required; no partial promotion or new futility rule. N24>=10/20 and>=C0/Q0 total, with substantive QD/ED and all existing gates. Native N24 rescue audit is profile-bound, including deletion-of-all-markers rejection; no rescue activation minimum beyond the frozen scientific protocol. Use original worker/in-process CUDA arithmetic and original evidence gates, charging full worker lifetime and auxiliary work. CPU supervisor consumes immutable receipts and never redoes a separate GPU audit.
+
+Report full outcomes/paired gains/losses, first-attempt and accepted-cell denominators, all invalid/recovery costs, exposure metadata and honest partial logical API/token accounting. Protected task/seed outcomes cannot become tuning inputs. Root consumes aggregate disposition for future mechanism decisions. If validated, prepare the original fixed10-task candidate/C0/Q0 formal acceptance and compute-matched substantive-QD-replacement ablation, separately frozen. Formal remains closed. Overall target still requires that final acceptance and reproducible delivery.
+
+## Provider and CPU boundary
+
+Stage exclusively current managed Codex ChatGPT login, frozen gpt-6-astra/low/E2/180s and public invocation. No Poe/fallback, no new guidance/grounding API, no credential inspection/copy/hash. Saved Poe credentials are retained untouched.
+
+CPU executor may create an isolated validation_implementation under this N24 folder, based exactly on3b7afa0, and non-executable drafts/templates. No owning-worktree source/state/ledger/locks/Arbor modifications, actual Dev/live or protected outcome reads, CUDA/model/API/simulator calls or GPU probe. Synthetic fixtures, two CPU threads and the established filesystem/network/dispatch guard are mandatory. Existing N23 validation implementation is a source-code reference only; its authority and failed candidate cannot be reused. Actual Dev promotion, root review/source integration, fresh identities/capacity proof, adopted protected authority and separate release are necessary before execution.
